  "worked_solution": "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P\u21d4Q$ is true if $P\u21d2Q$ **and** $Q\u21d2P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P\u21d4Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add columns for $\u00acY$ and $\u00acY\u2228X:$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,\u00acY\\,$ | $\\,\u00acY\u2228X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $X\u21d4(\u00acY\u2228X):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,\u00acY\\,$ | $\\,\u00acY\u2228X\\,$ | $\\,X\u21d4(\u00acY\u2228X)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
